{"tool_name":"netme","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"netme","home":"https://netme.click/","license":"Not licensed","summary":"On-the-fly knowledge network construction from biomedical literature.","addition_date":"2022-06-15T09:40:40.288825Z","last_update_date":"2022-06-15T09:40:40.291377Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:netme","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"alfredo.pulvirenti@unict.it","name":"Alfredo Pulvirenti","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Alessandro Muscolino"},{"name":"Alfredo Ferro"},{"name":"Antonio Di Maria"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Bibliography generation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3349"},{"term":"Information extraction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3907"},{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Relation extraction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3625"}]}],"name":"NETME","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/S41109-021-00435-X","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Background: The rapidly increasing biological literature is a key resource to automatically extract and gain knowledge concerning biological elements and their relations. Knowledge Networks are helpful tools in the context of biological knowledge discovery and modeling. Results: We introduce a novel system called NETME, which, starting from a set of full-texts obtained from PubMed, through an easy-to-use web interface, interactively extracts biological elements from ontological databases and then synthesizes a network inferring relations among such elements. The results clearly show that our tool is capable of inferring comprehensive and reliable biological networks.","authors":[{"name":"Alaimo S."},{"name":"Bellomo L."},{"name":"Billeci F."},{"name":"Borzi S."},{"name":"Di Maria